WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.997
This is the first runnable PostgreSQL example

00:00:03.024 --> 00:00:06.405
in the module Do not try to

00:00:06.418 --> 00:00:09.144
memorize it Read it from top to

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:11.184
bottom and identify the purpose of each

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:15.412
statement The first statement removes an earlier

00:00:15.439 --> 00:00:17.320
practice table if it exists so the

00:00:17.346 --> 00:00:20.520
example is safe to run again CREATE

00:00:20.546 --> 00:00:24.060
TABLE defines a small table INSERT INTO

00:00:24.073 --> 00:00:27.323
adds one row SELECT reads the rows

00:00:27.349 --> 00:00:31.373
back Before you click Run predict the

00:00:31.386 --> 00:00:34.560
final output You should expect one row

00:00:34.573 --> 00:00:36.468
with the patient ID and patient name

00:00:36.494 --> 00:00:40.424
that were inserted Run the code directly

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:42.424
in the browser and inspect the result

00:00:43.348 --> 00:00:45.374
Then if you want copy it into

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:47.585
pgAdmin's Query Tool and run the same

00:00:47.611 --> 00:00:51.663
three-step sequence there The goal is simply

00:00:51.689 --> 00:00:54.110
to connect CREATE INSERT and SELECT with

00:00:54.136 --> 00:00:55.149
what each one does
